      "source": [
        "## 3. Generar una población\n",
        "\n",
        "Una población es una lista de candidatos. Muestreamos cada gen dentro de su dominio, incluidos los extremos. El muestreo no garantiza capacidad: la función de aptitud ordena también los candidatos infactibles. Fijamos la semilla para reproducir esta demostración."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "id": "8cc2cb07",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.193258Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.192986Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.205081Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.204435Z"
        },
        "id": "8cc2cb07",
        "outputId": "7606d889-f270-41ab-a3e2-e53d8002bf38"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[0 6 4 3] 0.7382561362967388\n",
            "[3 7 0 6] 0.5662526744017468\n",
            "[1 0 3 8] 0.6852825530157587\n",
            "[6 6 5 7] 0.38248008751389373\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def random_individual(rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Sample one valid discrete chromosome; capacity is checked by evaluate.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return rng.integers(0, LIMITS + 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "rng_demo = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
        "population_demo = [random_individual(rng_demo) for _ in range(4)]\n",
        "for genes in population_demo:\n",
        "    print(genes, evaluate(genes)[\"fitness\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f678c6ed",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f678c6ed"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Seleccionar padres mediante torneo\n",
        "\n",
        "Tomamos dos candidatos distintos al azar y elegimos el de menor $F$. Repetimos para elegir otro padre; un mismo individuo puede ganar varios torneos. La selección favorece aptitudes bajas sin ordenar siempre toda la población. Devolvemos una copia para proteger el original."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "id": "9cc48ae0",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.206702Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.206511Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.211837Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.210622Z"
        },
        "id": "9cc48ae0",
        "outputId": "57fd1be4-f11b-4f10-e49c-9a1a20fbf6a4"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[3 7 0 6] [3 7 0 6]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def tournament(population: list, rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return an independent copy of the better of two sampled individuals.\"\"\"\n",
        "    indices = rng.choice(len(population), size=2, replace=False)\n",
        "    winner = min((population[i] for i in indices), key=lambda x: evaluate(x)[\"fitness\"])\n",
        "    return winner.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "parent_a = tournament(population_demo, rng_demo)\n",
        "parent_b = tournament(population_demo, rng_demo)\n",
        "print(parent_a, parent_b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f6ac5640",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f6ac5640"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Combinar información con cruza de un punto\n",
        "\n",
        "Elegimos un corte entre posiciones y tomamos el inicio del primer padre y el final del segundo. Conservamos la posición de cada edificio. Con padres $(6,6,6,6)$ y $(8,2,4,3)$ y corte 2 obtenemos $(6,6,4,3)$. La cruza preserva dominios, pero puede producir exceso de capacidad."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 12,
      "id": "541f462c",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.213455Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.213275Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.219581Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.218338Z"
        },
        "id": "541f462c",
        "outputId": "fa7de66b-76a7-4819-aa9d-9302a37ce5e2"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[3 7 0 6] {'treated': 987.3, 'potable': 1288.91, 'excess': 0.0, 'feasible': True, 'fitness': 0.5662526744017468}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def crossover(parent_a: np.ndarray, parent_b: np.ndarray,\n",
        "              rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Create one child using a cut between genes and preserving their positions.\"\"\"\n",
        "    cut = int(rng.integers(1, len(LIMITS)))\n",
        "    return np.concatenate((parent_a[:cut], parent_b[cut:]))\n",
        "\n",
        "child_demo = crossover(parent_a, parent_b, rng_demo)\n",
        "print(child_demo, evaluate(child_demo))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "17432bac",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "17432bac"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 6. Introducir variación con mutación\n",
        "\n",
        "Aplicamos la probabilidad a cada gen, no al cromosoma completo. Cada gen elegido sube o baja un nivel válido. En cero sólo subimos; en el máximo sólo bajamos. Con $p=0.25$ y cuatro genes, esperamos un gen seleccionado por hijo en promedio, no exactamente uno. La mutación puede mejorar o empeorar la aptitud."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 13,
      "id": "f8d7f236",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.221276Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.221106Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.225977Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-08T15:30:00.225020Z"
        },
        "id": "f8d7f236",
        "outputId": "087651bf-6c26-4378-aa87-8763c100634c"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "[3 7 0 6] [3 7 0 7] {'treated': 1055.6, 'potable': 1220.6100000000001, 'excess': 0.0, 'feasible': True, 'fitness': 0.5362466556249205}\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def mutate(child: np.ndarray, probability: float,\n",
        "           rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Independently move each selected gene one valid discrete step.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if not 0 <= probability <= 1:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\"Mutation probability must be between zero and one.\")\n",
        "    result = child.copy()\n",
        "    for i, limit in enumerate(LIMITS):\n",
        "        if rng.random() < probability:\n",
        "            neighbors = [v for v in (result[i] - 1, result[i] + 1) if 0 <= v <= limit]\n",
        "            result[i] = rng.choice(neighbors)\n",
        "    return result\n",
        "\n",
        "mutated_demo = mutate(child_demo, 0.25, rng_demo)\n",
        "print(child_demo, mutated_demo, evaluate(mutated_demo))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ac7a3847",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ac7a3847"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Reemplazar la población y conservar una élite\n",
        "\n",
        "Copiamos el mejor individuo sin modificarlo y llenamos las posiciones restantes con hijos. Mantenemos el tamaño de la población. El elitismo evita perder el mejor valor de aptitud; no demuestra que ya encontramos el óptimo. Con una copia independiente, mutar un hijo no modifica al padre ni a la élite."
      ]
    },
